Comments:
1. Evaluator: Kiana Setoodehnia, February 14, 2025. 
2. The spin-parities and energies of the resonances are evaluated by K. Setoodehnia based on D. R. Tilley et al., Nucl. Phys. A 636 (1998) 249 and the available 
   articles in the XUNDL database.  
3. The spectroscopic factor for the 663-keV resonance with J^Pi=3- is from H. T. Fortune and R. R. Betts, Phys. Rev. C 10 (1974) 1292.
4. The gamma-ray partial widths for the resonances come from those of the mirror state scaled for the 20Na resonance energies. The half-lives of the mirror states 
   are from D. R. Tilley, C. Cheves, J. Kelley, S. Raman, and H. Weller, Nucl. Phys. A 636 (1998) 249.  
5. The proton widths are measured by R. Coszach et al., Phys. Rev. C 50 (1994) 1695 for the 797-keV and 888-keV resonances, and by J. Belarge et al.,
   Phys. Rev. Lett. 117 (2016) 182701 for the 888-keV resonance.
6. The energy and strength for the 456-keV resonance was directly measured by R. Wilkinson et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 119 (2017) 242701.
7. The experimental rate agrees with the TALYS rate at 10 GK within the uncertainties. Therefore, no high-temperature rate matching is needed.
